WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.950
Tell mum: stay here, Ruža, when we say: wait for me at home.

2
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.450
There really is no milk.

3
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.850
Hello, Jovanka, did Ruža perhaps come to you?

4
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.950
No, I don't know what's going on.

5
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.660
Okay, fine, I won't panic.

6
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.950
Never mind, maybe she went out, I see there's no milk.

7
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.450
Okay, Jovanka, deal. Bye, don't worry, bye.

8
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.520
Mum, where are you?

9
00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.850
Where are you, my dear mummy?

10
00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.900
I'll call the police.

11
00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:19.850
I'll call the police, I don't care.

12
00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.550
This is a machine, okay, zero.

13
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.850
Come on, pick up, operator.

14
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.240
Hello, good afternoon!

15
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:38.230
I'd like to report my mother missing, please.

16
00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.050
Yes, I'm of age.

17
00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:52.940
Where have you been?

18
00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.560
I was out for a walk.

19
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.640
You were out for a walk?

20
00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.980
You went out for milk, you've been gone three hours.

21
00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.130
What, there's no milk? Good grief, you could have told me.

22
00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.520
It would have been on my way.

23
00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.800
I'm going to make you lunch, I'm in a hurry.

24
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.040
I've been telling you for three days, Ruža: a phone doesn't belong in the fridge, don't put it there.

25
00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.280
Anyway, it doesn't matter, they will bring it.

26
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.790
Who is "they"?

27
00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.140
Shh, what are those voices?

28
00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.280
It's me talking to you.

29
00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:39.710
No, no, no. I hear some little voice.

30
00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.400
Oh, Mum, you hear voices — what does that voice tell you?

31
00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:50.050
Well, it says something like: hello, hello, is anybody there?

32
00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.320
Goodness, I hear it too.

33
00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.910
Hello, is anybody there?

34
00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:04.430
See, Milentije, how absent-minded you are — I'll go make two cups of white coffee.

35
00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.460
Sorry, please, I completely forgot you were still on the line, and my mum came back.

36
00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:13.850
She goes out, then forgets where, you understand, she doesn't remember.

37
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.160
To prison.

38
00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.670
Please don't, madam.

39
00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.270
Oh, you are a gentleman, sorry.

40
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:27.980
Oh, Ruža!

41
00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:28.900
Where are you going?

42
00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.500
I can't make white coffee without milk.

43
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.430
I'm just going round the corner.

44
00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.330
You're not going anywhere. Stay right here!

45
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.370
Oh, you, sorry for interrupting, it's because she wants to leave, my mother, and then I'd have to look for her.

46
00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.030
Hello?

47
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.610
Huh? The police?

48
00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.100
Why are you calling us?

49
00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:04.160
Oh, it wasn't you who called, but my son?

50
00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.040
Well, he's fine, fine.

51
00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:10.710
Yes, he is. Thanks for asking.

52
00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.250
Do you have children?

53
00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.440
Ah, two.

54
00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:29.530
Yes, me too. Well, what can you do? Kids are kids. But I also have another son, you know. He's a famous cosmetic surgeon.

55
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:44.710
His name is Beba, that's what I call him. Well, he's stopped wetting the bed, yes, I really hope so.

56
00:05:44.760 --> 00:06:04.430
No, he isn't losing his mind. He's just, you know, a bit upset, but that's because his wife left him.

57
00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.010
Well, that I don't know.

58
00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.670
I don't know whether he abused her, no.

59
00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.260
Thank you, you are very kind.

60
00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.830
Sure, I'll get in touch, yes.

61
00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:19.690
I'll like you on Facebook, yes.

62
00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:20.510
What?

63
00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.430
Ah, the Serbian Ministry of Interior, okay, thanks.

64
00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.030
All the best, all the best.

65
00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.760
Thanks a lot, really.

66
00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:40.990
Now the whole police force knows my wife left me, and that I might have abused her.

67
00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.350
Beba.

68
00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.240
What is it?

69
00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:48.100
Tell me, you don't wet the bed anymore?

70
00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:48.490
No.

71
00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:55.010
Well, don't, son, you shouldn't at your age.

72
00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.800
Listen, my car broke down.

73
00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.750
Oh, when I remember how Dad used to maintain it.

74
00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.600
Yes, the first twenty years, then he let it go a bit.

75
00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.010
And you, son, have let yourself go a bit too.

76
00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:12.680
Look.

77
00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:17.030
I want that when I go out of here and come back, I find you here in this chair.

78
00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.210
Please. Don't go anywhere, don't buy anything, don't do anything.

79
00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.500
Enjoy the house, potter about here and there.

80
00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.550
Don't, please. There.

81
00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.830
Actually, I'm not asking you, I'm ordering you.

82
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.870
So we're agreed.

83
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:28.790
Clear.

84
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.250
Did we really agree?

85
00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:30.790
Well, of course.

86
00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:34.790
I don't want to.

87
00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:35.990
Fine.

88
00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:36.990
I'm going.

89
00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.850
Where are you going?

90
00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.580
I bought 12 litres of milk.

91
00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.350
Oh no, I wanted to go for milk.

92
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.700
You said yourself that you'd buy it.

93
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.200
To wait for them at the door.

94
00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.130
Who is "them"?

95
00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.350
Well, I don't know it all exactly.

96
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.840
Ruža, who are they?

97
00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.340
Well, I'm telling you, I don't know exactly.

98
00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.810
Come on, please, let's go to the dining room so you can tell me properly in a serious conversation.

99
00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.900
Who are the ones you're waiting for?

100
00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.770
What did they mention to you?

101
00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.140
Did they mention astral flights?

102
00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.440
Did they mention flying saucers?

103
00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.390
Did they mention the third eye?

104
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.340
Are they Jehovah's Witnesses?

105
00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.610
And did they mention some X-Files, something like that?

106
00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:44.960
No.

107
00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:47.820
Well, nothing, we have a nice chat.

108
00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.490
Yes, they are very kind.

109
00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:51.780
And what do they tell you?

110
00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.360
Well, they tell me what I ask them.

111
00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:58.960
No, I'm just thinking, maybe they didn't plan to abduct you.

112
00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:03.360
Good Lord, Milentije, what nonsense are you talking? What's wrong with you, son?

113
00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:06.480
They want to come here, not for you to go there.

114
00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.960
But where would I go, Beba, where?

115
00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:18.600
I'm telling you, they are very kind, they talk to me very nicely, they always say: good afternoon, madam, how are you today?

116
00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:25.830
And haven't you seen, when they come, say when they address you, some ray of light, a beam of light from the sky?

117
00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.520
Oh, what rubbish.

118
00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:34.850
And tell me, Ruža, did they come here when I was here?

119
00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:35.270
No.

120
00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.920
Listen, it would be best if you hid.

121
00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:46.280
Where?

122
00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.270
Well, in the wardrobe.

123
00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:50.230
Oh, great! Brilliant!

124
00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.560
Do you know how long we haven't played hide-and-seek?

125
00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:54.730
Oh, for years!

126
00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.730
Here, I'm closing my eyes and I'll count to a hundred in fives.

127
00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.090
Good afternoon!

128
00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:51.650
How are you today!

129
00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.050
Somebody brought you milk?

130
00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:59.210
Oh, that's the neighbour. He has a cat, you know, she's so greedy.

131
00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.230
You won't believe it, all this milk is for her.

132
00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:12.670
How wonderful you are, always selflessly helping people, Granny Ruža.

133
00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.030
How's the leg today?

134
00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:18.640
Oh, not at all. You know, I think it will never heal.

135
00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.170
Are you doing those little exercises I showed you?

136
00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.430
That quadriceps is about to atrophy.

137
00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.410
By the way, I'm not alone.

138
00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:40.150
I hope that's not a problem.

139
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.620
You have a visitor?

140
00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:43.430
My son is here.

141
00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.810
Oh, where? I don't see him.

142
00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:47.720
He's in the wardrobe.

143
00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.390
He's so infantile.

144
00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:55.790
And then suddenly he gets this urge and says: Mummy, Mummy, I want to be invisible.

145
00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.470
And then he hides in the wardrobe.

146
00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.210
Oh, how lovely, how old is the little one?

147
00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.500
Forty, yes.

148
00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:06.750
Son, come on, come out, darling, it's rude.

149
00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:10.350
He's very shy. His wife left him.

150
00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.620
I can't see you. Where are you?

151
00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:27.150
I'm here.

152
00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:32.710
Here? Okay, I came to help your mother, since she injured her leg.

153
00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.100
Which leg did she injure?

154
00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.910
Yes, and what are you saying? You know very well when I injured my leg.

155
00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:39.430
I don't know.

156
00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.140
Are you all right?

157
00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:41.370
No.

158
00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:42.790
Do I see you?

159
00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.760
I don't know. Do you see me, I'm here. What's going on here?

160
00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:49.450
That's exactly what I wanted to ask you.

161
00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.140
You know, you should visit your mother more often, sir.

162
00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:59.120
You know, I'm from the non-governmental organisation Let's Help the Elderly, and we help people like your mother.

163
00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.250
And what kind of people are like my mother?

164
00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.750
Well, if you visited her, you would see what a helpless little old lady she is.

165
00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.080
See how she likes it. If you visited her more often, you would know.

166
00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:15.370
Look, I don't visit my mother at all.

167
00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.570
And I noticed that.

168
00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.490
I live with her.

169
00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:18.570
In the wardrobe.

170
00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:25.640
No, I got into the wardrobe because she claims you won't come unless I get into the wardrobe. I got into the wardrobe so that you would come.

171
00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:29.010
In any case, I'm here, she's here, the wardrobe's here, you're here.

172
00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.470
You need help.

173
00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:36.810
Feel free to call this number, here you are, and everything will be fine.

174
00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.150
Goodbye, I kiss you, Ruža.

175
00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.730
Bye-bye, darling, bye-bye.

176
00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:41.650
I kiss you.

177
00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:45.760
Please, just a minute, just a minute.

178
00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:50.660
There is some logical explanation for everything, you know.

179
00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:58.170
My mum came today and claimed that she is friends with aliens.

180
00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:01.930
And that's why I bought 12 litres of milk.

181
00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.430
You see, we sat there and talked about it.

182
00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:11.290
I asked her whether she talks to them, and she said they would come here if I'm not around.

183
00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:16.660
So I got into the wardrobe to fulfil her wish that this certain alien comes.

184
00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:20.530
And partly to see whether he would come, because I'm an adventurer by nature.

185
00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:21.690
Clear.

186
00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:31.350
You surely think now that I'm an idiot coming out of a wardrobe?

187
00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.480
Of course... not.

188
00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:35.070
But there is a logical explanation for everything.

189
00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.810
You see, her leg doesn't hurt.

190
00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.880
She made it up. She's acting.

191
00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:49.150
She's fit as a fiddle.

192
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.010
She has legs like an antelope, literally.

193
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.490
She's healthy, really healthy.

194
00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.490
Clear, clear.

195
00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.910
She's cute.

196
00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:18.640
Mica is really cute, isn't she?

197
00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.720
She thinks I'm crazy?

198
00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:26.210
Well, son, that can be fixed.

199
00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:33.700
And why did you act like a poor tormented woman harassed by a crazy son from the wardrobe?

200
00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.130
I think she likes you.

201
00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:35.450
Oh, come on.

202
00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:44.810
How long have you been calling the organisation Let's Help the Elderly?

203
00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:47.830
Yes, I found them on Facebook the other day when I hurt my leg.

204
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.800
Oh come on, you hurt your leg six months ago and it healed in two days.

205
00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:57.180
Really? Look how time flies, I thought it was yesterday.

206
00:15:57.230 --> 00:16:00.410
But they've been bringing you lunch for six months.

207
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.000
Oh no, for goodness' sake. Maybe five.

208
00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:06.480
So what do you do with the lunch that I cook for you?

209
00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.520
And why are you counting my bites? Why?

210
00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.300
Oh, sorry.

211
00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:15.780
Well, never mind. I still like it much more when you cook.

212
00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:21.640
But why do you call them? You don't need help.

213
00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.580
You have me, I'm here.

214
00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:33.130
I like it when someone comes to visit me and then asks how I am and so on.

215
00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.230
A social worker is coming.

216
00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:03.550
There, you see. You see, you should have behaved sensibly,

217
00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.820
not got us into this kind of mess.

218
00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.380
But you lied to a humanitarian organisation, Mum.

219
00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:13.210
What do you think will happen to you when they find out what you did?

220
00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.750
Well, why would they find out?

221
00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.820
You'll go to prison!

222
00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:52.620
I think I haven't read this newspaper, look at this.

223
00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.330
You've read it three times.

224
00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:59.780
Oh look, Novak Đoković has entered the top hundred.

225
00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:06.390
Why are you throwing out those newspapers, they'll probably let me read them in prison.

226
00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.620
Don't worry about anything. You won't go to prison.

227
00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.960
I exaggerated a bit.

228
00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:13.280
Although you really did lie to a non-governmental organisation.

229
00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.170
That's for sure.

230
00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.330
I'll explain to them what a lonely person I am.

231
00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.840
Oh, my heart is breaking.

232
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:22.070
Look, you won't go to prison, Mum.

233
00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:25.020
But maybe they'll decide to send you to a nursing home.

234
00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.670
Ah, so that's where the rabbit is hiding.

235
00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.260
So that's what all this fuss is about.

236
00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:32.950
Shame on you.

237
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.250
Well, I'm not going to a nursing home, I won't, I won't and I won't.

238
00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.010
Okay, you won't go to a nursing home, don't worry.

239
00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.930
Just be normal now when they come.

240
00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.150
Who's coming?

241
00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.530
Social services.

242
00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:44.580
Oh, because of the leg?

243
00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:46.530
No, because of your memory, Ruža.

244
00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:51.410
What do you mean because of memory? My memory is excellent, what are you saying?

245
00:18:52.440 --> 00:19:02.350
Listen, when they arrive, we'll say that this worker came, that you cleaned all of this up yourself.

246
00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:05.280
Oh, no chance, son. No chance, Beba.

247
00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:10.750
They won't believe it, because if I had cleaned, this would look much better.

248
00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:15.340
The only thing you've cleaned is the window with your friend Tita.

249
00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:18.200
So what? But okay, that's not important.

250
00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:22.270
What matters is that when I clean, I clean perfectly.

251
00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:25.820
Here they are.

252
00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:26.790
Come on.

253
00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:36.630
Come on, just pretend you're normal.

254
00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:58.380
Good afternoon.

255
00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.140
Good afternoon.

256
00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:02.040
I'm Dragana, we spoke on the phone.

257
00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:06.480
Please, come in.

258
00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:07.170
Nice.

259
00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.240
Oh, it's a lovely flat.

260
00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:13.800
I vacuumed, I won't go to a nursing home, I won't.

261
00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.500
No, don't worry, Mum, you won't go to a nursing home. You sit here.

262
00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.960
Oh, thank you very much.

263
00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.990
You are a Miss?

264
00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:29.230
Radović, yes, but call me Dragana.

265
00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.920
But you are a Miss?

266
00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:32.820
I am.

267
00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:42.290
You know, Ruža, today I spoke with Milica from the organisation Let's Help the Elderly

268
00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:46.140
and she told me, I mean, she sounded somehow worried.

269
00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:04.030
I mean, Milica thought that you live alone,

270
00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.040
but your son is here too.

271
00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:16.000
I'll give you a form now to fill in.

272
00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:16.900
Here, please.

273
00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:30.260
Mr Beba, you understand that Let's Help the Elderly is an organisation that helps people who have no other help.

274
00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.210
Of course I understand, yes.

275
00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:38.840
What I don't understand at this moment is why your son doesn't make you lunch.

276
00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:43.270
Beba, don't talk nonsense.

277
00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:48.410
Mr Beba, I'm sure he would like to make you lunch every day.

278
00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:53.000
No, I didn't mean that. I'm telling you that I make lunch every day.

279
00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:55.740
I clean here, cook, wash, do everything.

280
00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:02.220
You've forgotten everything.

281
00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:07.680
I vacuumed, I cleaned, I threw out old newspapers,

282
00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:10.960
which isn't easy at all with a leg like this.

283
00:22:11.150 --> 00:22:12.840
But your leg is healthy.

284
00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:14.910
Well, you see what he's like.

285
00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:17.060
My spine could break,

286
00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:20.040
and he'd say I'm perfectly fine.

287
00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:24.900
I'll go make some white coffee.

288
00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:25.730
Lovely.

289
00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:29.330
If I even still have any milk.

290
00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.490
I'm sometimes, you know, so nervous.

291
00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:57.040
I mean, I cook, wash, clean, work here.

292
00:22:57.090 --> 00:23:00.520
She's difficult, always dissatisfied. I can't please her.

293
00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:01.780
You can't do everything alone.

294
00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:02.230
Exactly.

295
00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:02.960
And you're trying.

296
00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:07.380
Exactly. Bravo. You see, you are the first person I can talk to about this.

297
00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:09.030
What are you doing on Tuesday evening?

298
00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:10.620
What do you mean? In what capacity?

299
00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:18.640
How wonderful to have initiative.

300
00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:21.040
Commendable. That is very commendable.

301
00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:31.090
So, don't worry.

302
00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:38.540
I'll tell Milica to bring two lunches from now on.

303
00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:41.620
So, I'm leaving now.

304
00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.580
Beba, she likes you.

305
00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.840
Listen, she's a very perceptive woman.

306
00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:11.110
She understands everything.

307
00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.760
A real social worker.

308
00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:17.760
She told me that this Milica will bring us two lunches.

309
00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.470
Well, I'm telling you she likes you.

310
00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:20.770
And listen, that's great.

311
00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:23.600
Then you and I can have lunch together every day.

312
00:25:01.650 --> 00:25:06.330
Son, I have something very important to tell you.

313
00:25:06.380 --> 00:25:14.600
They will bring us lunch and from now on Beba and I will always eat together.
